DDEEPPRREECCAATTIIOONN NNOOTTIICCEE
     bbssddllaabbeell is deprecated and is not available in FreeBSD 15.0 or later.
     Use gpart(8) instead (with the BBSSDD partitioning scheme), or install the
     _f_r_e_e_b_s_d_-_b_s_d_l_a_b_e_l port or package.

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The bbssddllaabbeell utility installs, examines or modifies the BSD label on a
     disk partition, or on a file containing a partition image.  In addition,
     bbssddllaabbeell can install bootstrap code.

   DDiisskk DDeevviiccee NNaammee
     When specifying the device (i.e., when the --ff option is not used), the
     _/_d_e_v_/ path prefix may be omitted; the bbssddllaabbeell utility will automatically
     prepend it.

   GGeenneerraall OOppttiioonnss
     The --AA option enables processing of the historical parts of the BSD la‐
     bel.  If the option is not given, suitable values are set for these
     fields.

     The --ff option tells bbssddllaabbeell that the program will operate on a file in‐
     stead of a disk partition.

     The --nn option stops the bbssddllaabbeell program right before the disk would have
     been modified, and displays the result instead of writing it.

     The --mm _m_a_c_h_i_n_e argument forces bbssddllaabbeell to use a layout suitable for a
     different architecture.  Current valid values are ii338866 and aammdd6644.  If
     this option is omitted, bbssddllaabbeell will use a layout suitable for the cur‐
     rent machine.

